  "body": "**Blocked by:** #121\n\n## Context\n\nMCP connections are system resources similar to mailboxes, but secret material cannot live in item JSON.\n\n## Task\n\nSeed Semprec-owned system database `mcpServers` with name, strict connection configuration for `stdio`, `sse`, or `http`, `active`, `syncStatus`, and `lastSynced`. Extend `external_credentials` ownership to MCP server items and use the existing credentials package for encryption/decryption. Extend Processing proposal confirmation for database target `mcpServers`: Semp may propose non-secret name/config, while a logged-in human supplies the credential separately during the same confirmation transaction. Proposal JSON must reject credential fields. Neither proposal nor agent paths may synchronize tools.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Database seed, transport config validation, credential ownership, and proposal/confirm integration.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Tool discovery, grants, invocation, and new encryption design.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No plaintext credential appears in items, proposal history, or logs.\n- Confirm atomically stores server and encrypted credential or neither.\n- Agents can propose server metadata but cannot provide secrets or sync.\n",
